# HealthBinder

Local-first personal health record. One patient, one SQLite DB, runs locally. Not a medical device.

## Hard rules

- All DB access via Drizzle ORM — no raw SQL except in `apps/server/src/db/index.ts`
- AI-extracted facts (`extracted_facts` table) must never be written to canonical tables (`conditions`, `medications`, `labs`, etc.) without `user_confirmed = true`
- Single-tenant only — `getOrCreatePatient()` in `apps/server/src/index.ts` is the only patient access pattern
- No new npm dependencies without justification
- No comments explaining WHAT code does — only WHY if non-obvious

## Stack

- Backend: Hono + Drizzle + better-sqlite3 in `apps/server/`
- Frontend: React 18 + Vite + TailwindCSS + React Query in `apps/web/`
- Shared types live in `apps/web/src/api/client.ts` (interfaces) and `apps/server/src/db/schema.ts` (Drizzle tables)

## Patterns to follow

- New pages: `apps/web/src/pages/` → route in `App.tsx` → nav in `Layout.tsx` → i18n in `en.ts` + `ko.ts`
- New routes: add to `apps/server/src/index.ts` + typed function in `apps/web/src/api/client.ts`
- Country packs: `packages/country-packs/<code>/preventive-care.json` — seeder auto-picks up on restart
- Module triggers: `packages/clinical-rules/src/module-triggers.json`

## Medical content

Always include `source_url` and `version_date`. Use patient-facing language. Never state a diagnosis.

See `CLAUDE.md` and `CONTRIBUTING.md` for full details.
